# ============================================================================
# annotate landing — Night Desk direction — HERO, realistic variant (16:9)
# Model: nano banana (gemini / gemini-2.5-flash-image) — pinned below.
# AI-GENERATED MEDIA: output must be disclosed as AI-generated when published
# (caption, alt text, or credits line).
# Run: generate-media-prompt design/landing/prompts/night-desk/hero-realistic.media.prompt
# Replaces the abstract night-desk hero with a believable screenshot-style
# product shot: real-looking dark pricing page + annotate comment rail.
# Round 3: explicit string manifest, fewer distinct strings, rail docked.
# ============================================================================
schema: '0.4'

id: annotate-landing-nightdesk-hero-realistic
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Realistic product screenshot of a dark-themed SaaS pricing page in a clean
    flat browser window: three small window dots, address bar completely
    empty. Deep near-black background around the window with one
    soft warm ember glow behind it. The page is a modern dark UI: near-black
    canvas, slightly raised dark cards, hairline gray borders. Top-left heading
    "Simple pricing" with subheading "Pay for the team, not for seats".
    Below, three plan cards side by side. Left card: muted gray title
    "Starter" and muted price "$5" and nothing else. Right card: muted gray
    title "Pro" and muted price "$25" and nothing else. Center card is highlighted with a thin ember-orange
    border: title "Team" in orange, large price "$12", one gray line reading
    "per seat / month", two short feature lines "Unlimited comments" and
    "Email summaries", and a solid orange button "Start free trial". A crisp
    glowing ember-orange ring (soft warm bloom, the
    single brightest element in the scene) is drawn tightly around the words "per seat" within
    that "per seat / month" line — an annotation drawn over the existing words so
    they stay readable inside the ring, not a copy of them. A thin luminous orange connector line runs from the
    ring's right edge horizontally to a comment rail docked flush against the
    INSIDE right edge of the browser window. The rail is a dark raised panel with a
    hairline gray border and an almost-empty header bar with exactly two rounded comment cards. First
    card: small circular avatar with initials "MK" on a muted orange-tinted
    background, name "Mara K.", timestamp "2m", comment text "Can we say
    \"per seat\" here?", and below it an indented reply: smaller avatar "DT",
    name "Devon T.", one line "Legal flagged it. Switch to per user." Second
    card: avatar "JS", name "Jonas S.", one line "Looks good otherwise."
    The page uses EXACTLY these strings and no others: Simple pricing · Pay
    for the team, not for seats · Starter · $5 · Team · $12 · per seat /
    month · Pro · $25 · Unlimited comments · Email summaries · Start free
    trial · Mara K. · 2m · Can we say "per seat" here? · Devon T. · Legal
    flagged it. Switch to per user. · Jonas S. · Looks good otherwise. · MK ·
    DT · JS. All text crisp, correctly spelled, clean grotesque sans-serif,
    high contrast, no warping, no duplicated strings. Calm, precise,
    professional — believable enough to pass for a real app screenshot.
  negative: garbled glyphs, pseudo-letters, distorted or misspelled words,
    duplicated strings, hex color codes, hash symbols, any text in the rail
    header bar, any strings beyond the listed manifest, any URL or
    address-bar text, extra buttons or feature lines, watermarks, real brand
    logos, browser logo, photographic human faces, photorealistic people, a
    second glow color, neon signage, rainbow gradients, light theme,
    cluttered layout, lens flares, floating detached comment card, comment
    card overlapping the window edge, ring drawn as separate text
  style: believable UI product screenshot, dark-native flat design, crisp
    vector-sharp interface rendering, single warm ember accent, soft bloom,
    generous negative space around the window

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1344
    height: 768
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

requirements:
  subject: dark pricing page with ember ring on "per seat" and right-docked comment rail
  composition: browser window centered with margin, rail docked flush inside the window's right edge, ring focal on "per seat"
  palette: near-black canvas, dark UI surfaces, single ember accent #F97316
  do:
    - only the listed strings appear, spelled exactly
    - avatars are colored initials circles, never faces
    - ring hugs the existing "per seat" words, connector reaches the rail
  dont:
    - any URL, brand logo, or extra text
    - photographic humans
    - more than one accent hue

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  required_pass:
    - text_legibility
    - layout_realism
  criteria:
    text_legibility:
      weight: 3
      description: Every visible UI string matches the manifest, crisp and correctly spelled
      fail_signals:
        - garbled or pseudo-letter glyphs
        - warped, duplicated, or misspelled words
    layout_realism:
      weight: 3
      description: Believable pricing page; comment rail docked flush inside the window
      fail_signals:
        - floating detached panels
        - card overlapping the window frame
    ring_and_connection:
      weight: 2
      description: Ember ring hugs "per seat"; thin connector reaches the pinned comment
      fail_signals:
        - ring absent, misplaced, or rendered as its own text
        - connector detached or pointing at nothing
    palette_discipline:
      weight: 2
      description: Near-black canvas with a single warm ember accent
      fail_signals:
        - second glowing hue (blue, green, pink)
        - light theme or washed-out surfaces
  reject_if:
    - garbled or misspelled text anywhere in the UI
    - real brand logo, URL, or watermark
    - photographic human face
    - more than one glow color
    - comment card detached from the window edge

tags:
  - marketing
  - landing-hero
  - annotate
  - ai-generated
product_targets: [annotate.therobotlives.com]
